  "body": "Most implementations of the stream on the web platform won't actually want the ReadableStream and WritableStream constructors we propose. Instead they will expose the rest of the API, but have their own constructors. E.g.\n\n```\nclass StreamingWebSocket {\n  constructor(ToString endpoint);\n  mixin ReadableStream;\n  mixin WritableStream;\n}\n```\n\n``` js\nconst socket = new StreamingWebSocket(\"ws://example.com/endpoint\");\n\nsocket.read()\n  .then(x => console.log(x))\n  .catch(e => console.error(e));\n\nsocket.write(str2ab(\"i have data for you, server!\"))\n  .catch(e => console.error(e));\n```\n\nThis also makes duplex streams easy, as seen above.\n\nWe also need to make it easy to implement mixins in user-space, instead of just in spec-land where we can assume there are magic I/O mechanisms to push and pull data. This is a bit trickier because of how we have our constructors set up; it's not just \"overwrite this underscore-prefixed method\" like in Node.js.\n",
